## KernelComponentBase

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Models`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

### Purpose
Abstract base class for Blazor components that need access to the current Semantic Kernel instance and its services. Components extending this class receive the active kernel as a `[Parameter]`, and all properties marked with `[KernelInject]` are automatically resolved from `Kernel.Services` via reflection.

### Class Definition

```csharp
public abstract class KernelComponentBase : ComponentBase
{
    [Parameter]
    [EditorRequired]
#pragma warning disable BL0007 // Intentional: Kernel must be processed before OnInitialized.
    public Kernel Kernel
    {
        get { return _kernel; }
        set
        {
            _kernel = value;
            OnKernelSet();
        }
    }
#pragma warning restore BL0007
    private Kernel _kernel { get; set; } = default!;

    private void OnKernelSet()
    {
        var type = GetType();
        var props = type.GetProperties(
            BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.NonPublic);

        foreach (var prop in props)
        {
            var att = prop.GetCustomAttribute<KernelInjectAttribute>(inherit: true);
            if (att == null) continue;

            var setter = prop.SetMethod;
            if (setter == null)
                throw new InvalidOperationException($"{prop.Name} has no setter.");

            object? service;
            if (att.Key == null)
            {
                service = Kernel.Services.GetService(prop.PropertyType);
                if (service == null)
                    throw new InvalidOperationException($"Unable to find service of type {prop.PropertyType} in Kernel");
            }
            else
            {
                service = Kernel.Services.GetKeyedService(prop.PropertyType, att.Key);
                if (service == null)
                    throw new InvalidOperationException($"Unable to find keyed service of type {prop.PropertyType} with key '{att.Key}' in Kernel");
            }

            setter.Invoke(this, [service]);
        }
    }
}
```

### Properties

| Property | Type | Attributes | Description |
|----------|------|------------|-------------|
| `Kernel` | `Kernel` | `[Parameter]`, `[EditorRequired]` | The active Semantic Kernel instance for the current chat. Setter triggers `OnKernelSet()` for `[KernelInject]` resolution. |

### Injection Behavior
When `Kernel` is set (via parameter assignment):
1. Reflection scans all public and non-public instance properties
2. Properties with `[KernelInject]` are identified
3. For each marked property:
   - If `Key` is null: calls `Kernel.Services.GetService(prop.PropertyType)`
   - If `Key` is set: calls `Kernel.Services.GetKeyedService(prop.PropertyType, att.Key)`
4. Throws `InvalidOperationException` if service not found
5. Throws `InvalidOperationException` if property has no setter
6. Invokes the property setter with the resolved service

### Usage

Components must extend `KernelComponentBase` (not just `ComponentBase`) to be registered as toolbar components:

```csharp
public class MyToolbarComponent : KernelComponentBase
{
    [KernelInject]
    public IChatMessageService ChatService { get; set; } = default!;

    [KernelInject(Key = "my-key")]
    public IMyService MyService { get; set; } = default!;

    private void DoSomething()
    {
        // Access kernel services
        var history = ChatService.DisplayHistory;
    }
}
```

### Registration
Register toolbar components via `CyrenaKernelBuilderExtensions`:
```csharp
builder.AddToolbarComponent<MyToolbarComponent>(ToolbarAlignment.End);
```

### Constraints
- The `Kernel` parameter is `[EditorRequired]` — the parent must provide it.
- Only components inheriting from `KernelComponentBase` can be registered with `AddToolbarComponent<TComponent>()`.
- Properties with `[KernelInject]` must have a public or non-public setter.
- Service resolution happens when `Kernel` is set, which may be before `OnInitialized`.

